"narrative": "No assessments are due, so this explore stage focuses on refining the remaining unresolved scientific questions rather than repeating the already accepted large effects. The highest-priority unresolved biological axis is TP53 status and MDM2 dependency: broad, adenocarcinoma, and Avana estimates have been small and imprecise. I therefore add library-context absolute estimates for Ky and Humagne_CD libraries, plus a library interaction test, because non-Avana cells are rare but could reveal either a technical dilution or a context-specific p53-MDM2 association. I also add biologically motivated signaling tests: PTEN loss versus STAT3 dependency, and a PIK3CA-by-PTEN-loss interaction for STAT3, to test whether PI3K pathway activation is associated with stronger STAT3 dependency either generally or in the PTEN-loss context. For the accepted USP7 association, I test CDKN2A loss among TP53 wild-type cells; if CDKN2A loss disrupts p53 pathway activity, it should associate with weaker USP7 dependency, which would refine the meaning of the TP53 wild-type finding beyond a simple gene-level p53 label. For SMARCA2, I test ARID1A loss conditional on SMARCA4 loss to examine whether co-occurring BAF complex alterations modify the strong SMARCA4-loss association. I add KRAS mutation effect within TP53-loss cells because the broad KRAS claim is unsupported but co-mutation context can still be scientifically informative. I add a Ky-library WRN check because MSI-high WRN is robust overall and in Avana; a Ky estimate can further test whether the association survives in a different library context. Finally, I test STK11 loss versus NFE2L2 dependency with the reversed weaker-dependency hypothesis because STK11/KEAP1-associated oxidative-stress pathway alterations may affect NFE2L2 dependency, but this remains exploratory.",
"research_notes": "Iteration 4 explore update. Accepted dataset associations remain strong: SMARCA4 loss with stronger SMARCA2 dependency; MSI-high with stronger WRN dependency; TP53 wild-type versus TP53 loss with stronger USP7 dependency; KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency. These are now supported broadly, in adenocarcinoma where applicable, and in Avana and non-Avana library contexts, plus independent validation for SMARCA2. Rejected or unsupported broad claims include KRAS/KRAS, BRAF V600E/BRAF, EGFR amplification/EGFR, MYC amplification effects on RPL11/POLR2A/DHX9, KRAS/RIT1, pure ERBB2/ERBB2, and ARID1A-independent SMARCA2. MDM2 remains the main unresolved small-effect question: broad, adenocarcinoma, and Avana estimates are small positive, below or near the approximate clinical benchmark, with intervals including null. Explore now adds Ky-library and Humagne_CD-library MDM2 absolute estimates and a TP53-by-Avana interaction to complete context-specific discovery for MDM2. PIK3CA/STAT3 is broadened with PTEN-loss biology: PTEN-loss main effect and PIK3CA-by-PTEN-loss interaction. USP7 is refined with CDKN2A loss among TP53 wild-type cells as a p53-pathway-status test. SMARCA2 is refined with ARID1A loss conditional on SMARCA4 loss. KRAS is refined in TP53-loss co-mutation context. WRN is refined in Ky library. STK11 loss versus NFE2L2 is an exploratory oxidative-stress pathway test. Validation remains conserved: current accepted effects are too large to need more validation, and MDM2 contexts should be completed in discovery before considering strict validation of borderline effects."
