"narrative":"No assessments are due, so I request twelve already registered analyses. The first priority is to finish resolving the weak, unresolved TP53-to-MDM2 association. Broad and Avana estimates have been small and imprecise, so I test the complementary non-Avana library context (H41), the adenocarcinoma-versus-non-adenocarcinoma interaction (H42), a CDKN2A-intact restriction (H50), and a direct CDKN2A-loss effect within TP53 wild-type cells (H51). CDKN2A is biologically relevant to p53 pathway integrity through ARF-MDM2, so these tests distinguish whether the weak broad signal is diluted by co-loss or is simply near null. Second, I broaden to mechanistically motivated marker-outcome hypotheses that have not been tested. PI3K pathway alteration could modify STAT3 dependency, so I run PIK3CA mutation versus STAT3 (H48), PTEN loss versus STAT3 broadly (H53), and PTEN loss versus STAT3 within PIK3CA wild-type cells (H54). Third, MAPK biology is tested with NF1 loss: direction -1 for KRAS, expecting stronger KRAS dependency if RAS pathway activation increases dependence on KRAS, and direction +1 for BRAF, expecting weaker BRAF dependency if NF1 loss provides alternative MAPK activation or bypasses BRAF. Fourth, I add secretory-pathway and oxidative-stress screens: ERBB2 amplification versus TMED10 (H49), APC mutation versus TMED10 (H60), and STK11 loss versus NFE2L2 with direction +1, which tests weaker NFE2L2 dependency as the primary direction. These choices avoid repeatedly testing the already robust large effects unless they are direct co-alteration refinements, and they prioritize the remaining borderline MDM2 context plus high-value new associations. All estimates will be assessed as associations in the supplied dataset, not as causal or externally generalizable claims.",
"research_notes":"Iteration 4 analyze selection. Run: MDM2 context completion H41 non-Avana, H42 lineage interaction, H50 CDKN2A-intact TP53 wt, H51 CDKN2A loss in TP53 wt. PI3K/STAT3 H48 PIK3CA, H53 PTEN broad, H54 PTEN in PIK3CA wt. MAPK/NF1 H57 KRAS and H58 BRAF. TMED10 screens H49 ERBB2 and H60 APC. Oxidative/NFE2L2 screen H59 STK11 with direction +1 testing weaker NFE2L2 dependency. Deferred for now: SMARCA2 co-loss in SMARCA4-loss H55/H56, USP7 CDKN2A context H52, KRAS adenocarcinoma H39, pure BRAF H29, ERBB2 broad contexts, and interactions for accepted large effects. Validation remains conserved for later; use only if a focused discovery set yields consistent near-threshold evidence, especially for MDM2 or STAT3. Interpret signed estimates: direction -1 positive means stronger dependency in exposed group; direction +1 positive means weaker dependency in exposed group."
}

