  "narrative": "No assessments are due at this exploration stage. I registered twelve follow-up comparisons to sharpen the current evidence. First, I added robustness checks for accepted or partially robust associations: MSI-high versus dependency_WRN in Ky-library screens and in DNA-complete lines, and TP53-wild-type versus TP53-loss versus dependency_USP7 in DNA-complete lines. These test whether the WRN and USP7 signals persist under a different screen library and when DNA genomic calls are present. Second, I registered co-alteration specificity checks for the major accepted clusters: SMARCA4 loss versus dependency_SMARCA2 within KEAP1-loss lines, TP53 status versus dependency_USP7 within KEAP1-loss lines, KEAP1 loss versus dependency_NFE2L2 within TP53-loss lines, MSI-high versus dependency_WRN within TP53-loss lines, PTEN loss versus dependency_STAT3 within STK11-loss lines, and CDKN2A loss versus dependency_MDM2 within KEAP1-loss and STK11-loss lines. These are falsifiable context tests: if the associations remain large and signed in the expected direction, they are less likely to be artifacts of a single linked co-alteration or a narrow genomic context. If they collapse toward zero or fall below approximately 10% relative clinical benchmarks for the relevant dependency score, I would qualify the association as context-dependent. I used approximate outcome-specific benchmarks near 0.042 for SMARCA2, 0.030 for WRN, 0.009 for USP7 and NFE2L2, 0.028 for STAT3, and 0.027 for MDM2. Third, I added two pure cross-driver KRAS/BRAF tests excluding EGFR and ERBB2 amplification: BRAF-V600E versus dependency_KRAS and KRAS mutation versus dependency_BRAF. Because driver-pathway activation can reduce dependency on an adjacent upstream or downstream kinase, I anticipated a positive signed contrast in these tests, meaning weaker dependency in the exposed driver-mutant group, but the broad driver-dependency nulls already observed make uncertainty high. All registered claims remain associations in this supplied dataset and do not establish causality or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 8 explore: current supported dataset clusters are SMARCA4 loss with much stronger dependency_SMARCA2; TP53 wild-type versus TP53 loss with much stronger dependency_USP7; KEAP1 loss with weaker dependency_NFE2L2; MSI-high with much stronger dependency_WRN; PTEN loss with much stronger dependency_STAT3; and CDKN2A loss with much stronger dependency_MDM2. Prior robustness includes adenocarcinoma, Avana, MTAP-loss, STK11-loss, PIK3CA-mutant, KEAP1-loss, CDKN2A-loss, higher-mutation-burden, marker-D-negative, and several independent validations. H100 PTEN-loss CDKN2A/MDM2 remains unresolved and deferred because validation was direction-consistent but imprecise. New registered priorities: WRN and USP7 library/DNA-complete checks, co-alteration specificity for accepted clusters, and two cross-driver KRAS/BRAF tests. If new context estimates remain far above benchmark, treat clusters as broadly applicable within this dataset; if attenuated, restrict claims to contexts already tested."
